# M5Atom Echo GPS Development Guidelines

## Model Context Protocol Directives

- When reviewing code, first understand the hardware limitations of the M5Atom Echo
- Always consider the limited GPIO availability on the M5Atom Echo platform
- When suggesting changes, ensure they are compatible with ESP32-PICO-D4 hardware
- For Serial communication, remember that M5Atom Echo has USB CDC serial issues requiring special configuration

## Serial Communication Guidelines

- Always use `serial_baudrate = 0` in M5.config() to disable default serial initialization
- Use these build flags for proper USB CDC operation:
  ```
  -D ARDUINO_USB_MODE=1
  -D ARDUINO_USB_CDC_ON_BOOT=1
  -D DISABLE_SERIAL=1
  -D DISABLE_SERIALEVENT=1
  ```
- For GPS module communication, use the separate UART interfaces:
  ```cpp
  // GPS module connections
  #define GPS_RX 22  // ESP32 RX pin connected to GPS TX
  #define GPS_TX 19  // ESP32 TX pin connected to GPS RX
  HardwareSerial GPS(1);  // Using UART1 for GPS
  GPS.begin(9600, SERIAL_8N1, GPS_RX, GPS_TX);
  ```
- For TTL converter/host communication:
  ```cpp
  // TTL to RS232 level converter connections
  #define HOST_RX 21  // ESP32 RX pin connected to TTL TX
  #define HOST_TX 25  // ESP32 TX pin connected to TTL RX
  HardwareSerial Host(2);  // Using UART2 for host communication
  Host.begin(9600, SERIAL_8N1, HOST_RX, HOST_TX);
  ```

## Pin Assignment Standards

- Use predefined constant names for pins:
  ```cpp
  // I2C pins - shared between compass and display
  #define I2C_SDA 26
  #define I2C_SCL 32
  
  // GPS module connections
  #define GPS_RX 22  // ESP32 RX pin connected to GPS TX
  #define GPS_TX 19  // ESP32 TX pin connected to GPS RX
  
  // TTL to RS232 level converter connections
  #define HOST_RX 21  // ESP32 RX pin connected to TTL TX
  #define HOST_TX 25  // ESP32 TX pin connected to TTL RX
  ```

## I2C Communication

- Initialize I2C before initializing any I2C devices:
  ```cpp
  // Initialize I2C for shared compass and display use
  Wire.begin(I2C_SDA, I2C_SCL);
  ```
- Remember that I2C bus is shared between the compass and the display
- Keep I2C commands efficient to avoid blocking the bus

## Library Configuration

- For M5Unified version 0.2.5:
  - Initialize with custom configuration to avoid Serial issues
  - Use display and audio functions through the M5 interface

## Coding Style

- Use 2-space indentation
- Use snake_case for variable and function names
- Prefer constants over magic numbers
- Add descriptive comments for hardware-specific code
- Document pin assignments clearly

## Project Structure

- src/ - Application code
- lib/ - Custom libraries
- .cursor/ - Cursor configuration 
- platformio.ini - PlatformIO configuration 